---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { SITE } from "../lib/site";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="GibTalk doesn't collect or store any of your data."
>
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 12 November 2026</p>

  <p>
    GibTalk doesn't collect or store any of your data, or track how you use it.
    There's no account, no login, no analytics, no advertising, and no cookies
    or unique identifiers.
  </p>

  <h2>Your words and pictures</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you add stays on your device: your words, their pictures and any
    photos you take. GibTalk works offline. Nothing is uploaded.
  </p>
  <p>
    The camera is used only when you take a photo for a word or scan the QR code
    of a shared set. What it sees stays on your device.
  </p>
  <p>
    Backups are files saved on your device. Where they go after that is up to
    you.
  </p>

  <h2>When GibTalk goes online</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Searching symbols</strong> sends your search words to the GibTalk
      symbols server (<code>api.gibtalk.com</code>; older versions of the app
      use <code>api-gibtalk.apps.bancuh.net</code>) and downloads the matching
      pictures. Searches aren't linked to you, and there's no account to link
      them to.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Templates</strong> are downloaded from the same symbols server (
      <code>api.gibtalk.com</code>) when you open the Templates screen, along
      with their pictures. Versions before 1.0.21 download them from GibTalk's
      public GitHub repository.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Opening a shared set</strong> downloads its pictures from the same
      server. The set itself is inside the link or QR code, so it isn't fetched
      from anywhere.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Speaking words</strong> uses your device's built-in
      text-to-speech.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    As with any website, those servers can see your IP address when your device
    downloads from them.
  </p>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    gibtalk.com has no analytics and no cookies. The symbol search on this site
    sends your search words to the same symbols server. The web app at
    app.gibtalk.com runs in your browser: the words and photos you add aren't
    uploaded, and your sets are kept only in your browser's storage. A share
    link carries the set inside the link itself, after the # sign, which
    browsers don't send to any server; it holds the words and symbols, never
    your photos. When the app on your phone opens a shared set, the same
    applies.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the new version will be posted here, with a new date
    at the top.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions? Email{" "}
    <a href={`mailto:${SITE.supportEmail}`}>{SITE.supportEmail}</a>
    or see the <a href="/support/">support page</a>.
  </p>
</Base>
